@davidly I saw the agent getting caught out a couple of times with invalid cpm names - it would silently crash/hang when running m80/l80 - now ntvcm validates names and will return a clear msg to the agent...

M80 and L80 parse their own command tail and silently crash (or corrupt memory) when handed a filename whose base name exceeds 8 characters or whose type exceeds 3 characters. Add a pre-launch check that tokenizes the command tail the way these tools do (splitting on space, ',' and '=', honoring 'X:' drive prefixes, and skipping L80 '/switches') and validates each filename token against CP/M's 8.3 rules.

When a token is not 8.3 compliant, ntvcm now prints a clear error naming the offending token and exits instead of letting the assembler or linker hang or crash. The check is scoped to m80.com and l80.com so other apps' command-line syntax is unaffected.

